 "_about": "Seconds each test file takes in one CI shard (setup + call + teardown, coverage on). scripts/ci_test_shards.py balances the shards on these; a file not listed weighs its test count times per_test_seconds_default. Measured 2026-09-28 per file from the shard reports of three CI runs (main run 36443202051 py3.13, PR #68 run 36476128848 py3.13, PR #69 run 36476376620 py3.12 and py3.13): each file's LARGEST measurement, so a slower runner or Python version never under-weighs it; per_test_seconds_default is PR #69's py3.13 seconds over its tests. The files split out of tests/test_factory_loop.py and tests/test_worker.py share their parent's measured seconds in proportion to one local run of the three. (The first table, 2026-09-27, spread each 72-test progress line's elapsed time evenly over its tests, which gave a slow file's seconds to its neighbours: P-740.) Refresh: download the test-shard-py* artifacts of one or more CI runs, both Python versions, and run `python3 scripts/ci_test_shards.py weights <every shard-*.json>`: it keeps each file's largest measurement, never a sum. The required test (py...) aggregators fail when the table goes stale.",
